      "id": 1,
      "text": "Bakersville was laid out in 1848 by John Baker, who gave the community his own name.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        1,
        22
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia",
        "Web source 2"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bakersville%2C_Ohio"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "A post office opened in Bakersville in 1850 and stayed open until 2002, serving the village for 152 years.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        7
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bakersville%2C_Ohio"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "The town sits in a picturesque valley along Evans Creek, northeast of West Lafayette on State Route 751.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        5,
        6
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bakersville%2C_Ohio"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "Shortly after its founding, a woolen factory operated in Bakersville for about six years, supplying local textiles.",
